# Frontend env (Vite)
#
# No runtime env vars are required for the v1 frontend — the API base URL
# is "/api" by convention, proxied to the backend in dev (via Vite's server.proxy
# in vite.config.ts) and served same-origin in prod (via nginx in
# frontend/nginx.conf).
#
# Vite only exposes env vars to the browser bundle when they're prefixed
# with `VITE_`. None are needed today. If you add one for v2 (e.g. a
# different API origin, feature flags, telemetry), declare it here so the
# next developer sees the contract:
#
#   VITE_API_BASE=http://localhost:3001/api
#   VITE_FEATURE_X=on
#
# Compose host-port + backend runtime env vars live in the repo-root
# .env.example.
